      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To neutralize anticipated pushback, frame any \"challenges\" not as legitimate problems, but as areas requiring necessary clarification or modernization. Instead of addressing \"cons,\" discuss \"implementation considerations,\" such as training needs or procedural updates. You can state that while some stakeholders may require time to adapt to evolving workplace norms, the policy's objective is to align with best practices for modern, equitable employment. This approach subtly frames resistance as a matter of adjustment, not a valid critique of the principle itself.",
